{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition","id":1369532,"title":"How broken are sidereal martial arts in second edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-22T01:34:12-08:00","id":1369532,"title":"How broken are sidereal martial arts in second edition?","content":"Are all styles broken? If yes, is there any way to fix them ? Such as increasing the minimum essence requirements a bit?<br /> <br /> Also, is it possible to use first edition's SMA instead, with some tweaking? I admit to knowing absolutely nothing about them save that many people in the forums think they were cool and more balanced than the 2E ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T02:26:33-08:00","id":1369538,"title":"","content":"Sidereal Martial Arts are already high Essence effects. No more broken than Essence 6+ Solar Charms. (Providing you're using the 2.5 Errata and can't just punch new Exalts into existence.)<br /> <br /> Solars must have a Sidereal tutor to learn SMA. And Sides have significantly fewer Essence-bump Charms. So if you wanted to use the Essence 4/5 Student Sutra Charms then they really won't affect your game that much.<br /> <br /> But I strongly advise you play 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T03:31:56-08:00","id":1369544,"title":"","content":"They\u2019re not just broken in the sense of \u201cinsanely powerful\u201d though. They\u2019re often broken in the sense of \u201cthis doesn\u2019t work the way it says it does.\u201d Many of their techniques were not compatible with combos. Some were obviously in need of other keywords and lacked them. <br /> <br /> Also, no SMA Charm cost sutra discount could ever be balanced against the Essence 6 SMA Charm that made them all <i>free</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-22-2020, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T04:06:46-08:00","id":1369546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition?p=1369538#post1369538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Martial Arts are already high Essence effects. No more broken than Essence 6+ Solar Charms. (Providing you're using the 2.5 Errata and can't just punch new Exalts into existence.)<br /> <br /> Solars must have a Sidereal tutor to learn SMA. And Sides have significantly fewer Essence-bump Charms. So if you wanted to use the Essence 4/5 Student Sutra Charms then they really won't affect your game that much.<br /> <br /> But I strongly advise you play 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they are not anymore broken than Essence 6+ solar charms, what's the problem? Aren't such charms supposed to be uber powerful anyway?<br /> <br /> Let's say, for example, that the dragonblooded could learn SMA like the bronze faction wants them to. <br /> How strong would this make them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition?p=1369544#post1369544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re not just broken in the sense of \u201cinsanely powerful\u201d though. They\u2019re often broken in the sense of \u201cthis doesn\u2019t work the way it says it does.\u201d Many of their techniques were not compatible with combos. Some were obviously in need of other keywords and lacked them.<br /> <br /> Also, no SMA Charm cost sutra discount could ever be balanced against the Essence 6 SMA Charm that made them all <i>free</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Can you give any examples? More of a sorcery/social person here... i just find it difficult to evaluate martial arts or similar abilities<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 02-22-2020, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T04:28:40-08:00","id":1369549,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be honest, I think that even from Jenna Moran, the assertion that Sidereal Martial Arts represented a standard for Essence 6 or higher powers for any Exalted was a bad addition to the game's discourse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T04:49:21-08:00","id":1369551,"title":"","content":"I want to say it was Obsidian Shards of Infinity that's capstone let you <i>decide the results of the fight. </i><br /> I remember one of them let you make essentially clones of yourself, and these clones had their own mote pools and charms. (or was it clones of your enemies.)<br /> And I distinctly remember one being key to the &quot;go to mount meru, and with one kick wipe out Creation&quot; meme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T04:52:40-08:00","id":1369553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition?p=1369546#post1369546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give any examples? More of a sorcery/social person here... i just find it difficult to evaluate martial arts or similar abilities</div> </div> </div> </div>IMPERSONAL PERSONAL DENATURE STING is an Essence 6 Shaping attack that lets you completely rewrite someone's Virtues.<br /> <br /> Only it's not. It doesn't have the Shaping keyword, so every single defense designed to protect you from having your Virtues rewritten simply doesn't work. You Perfect Dodge or you get your character sheet taken away.<br /> <br /> This is from Boarder of Kalideoscope Logic Style, which is one of the better written and least broken styles.<br /> <br /> But I honestly don't think that makes SMA unplayable. Impersonal Personal Denature Sting is VERY CLEARLY a Shaping attack, so just house-rule that it has the Shaping keyword and play it as written. It's not a big deal. Just use what 3E calls the Storyteller's Rule and everyone else calls &quot;common sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition?p=1369546#post1369546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are not anymore broken than Essence 6+ solar charms, what's the problem? </div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 6+ Solar Charms break the fundamental assumptions of the game, trivialize any narrative short of fighting all the Yozi at once and are generally grotesquely over-powered.<br /> <br /> I have one word for anyone who thinks SMA are worse: Zeal.<br /> <br /> If you're playing an E6+ game then expect to hotfix and houserule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition?p=1369546#post1369546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say, for example, that the dragonblooded could learn SMA like the bronze faction wants them to. <br /> How strong would this make them?</div> </div> </div> </div>My favourite 2E game gave SMA to five Dragon-Blooded after they got hit with (pre-Errata) Pattern Spider Touch to make them the behemoth-blooded children of the actual Elemental Dragons on top of being Breeding 6 Dragon-Blooded. Good times.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking SMA is on a par with Solar Charms of equivalent Essence. DBs have smaller mote pools so it's not an immediate bump, but it's about equal to making them Akuma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-22-2020, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T13:44:33-08:00","id":1369639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition?p=1369551#post1369551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I distinctly remember one being key to the &quot;go to mount meru, and with one kick wipe out Creation&quot; meme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the &quot;Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick&quot; relies on a combination of Grandmother Spider Mastery and Pattern Spider Touch, and...some means by which to actually <i>see</i> all of Creation from your vantage point on Mount Meru.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where anyone is supposed to get that last part. I don't think Sidereals actually have an Awareness Charm like that. In 1e (specifically Savage Seas, I just checked), there was a Solar Charm called Hundred Leagues Sight Procedure which could let you see absurdly far, but I don't think even that would get you a view of all Creation.<br /> <br /> A Solar with all those Charms could definitely wipe out everyone within (Essence * 20) miles in the direction they were looking, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T14:06:46-08:00","id":1369645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1369532-how-broken-are-sidereal-martial-arts-in-second-edition?p=1369639#post1369639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, the &amp;quot;Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick&amp;quot; relies on a combination of Grandmother Spider Mastery and Pattern Spider Touch, and...some means by which to actually <i>see</i> all of Creation from your vantage point on Mount Meru.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where anyone is supposed to get that last part. I don't think Sidereals actually have an Awareness Charm like that. In 1e (specifically Savage Seas, I just checked), there was a Solar Charm called Hundred Leagues Sight Procedure which could let you see absurdly far, but I don't think even that would get you a view of all Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a Storyteller willing to grant that seeing the world is equivalent to seeing all of the people in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write 